  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Welfare Support for Orphans in Tombura</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support up to 36 orphans and vulnerable children in the Diocese of Tombura- Yambio, through the building of permanent and secure accommodation.  It will also ensure that these children have food, clothes, school fees and learning materials and will support them through counselling and psycho-social support. 
Sister Bianca has been working in the Diocese of Tombura-Yambio, with orphans and vulnerable children, for over 30 years - throughout the civil war and the recent Lord&#x2019;s Resistance Army crisis in the region.  With little funding or support Sister Bianca has established a base in Tombura and is taking care of over 30 children with the help of some volunteer staff. There has been a recent call from the community and development partners to scale up this project.  CAFOD has a long standing relationship with our partner, CDTY (Catholic Diocese of Tombura-Yambio) supporting their HIV/AIDS work and we are looking to increase this support to other areas of their work.</narrative>
  </description>
